        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "835dc68e-c6c9-530f-9e6f-868d805c3ea1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham Bankier, Oskar Schindler\n- Companies: Rekord factory\n- Places: Lipowa Street, Cracow, Poland, occupied Poland, Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia\n- Roles: owner, industrialist, spy, Nazi Party member\n- Events: World War II, Holocaust\n\nFacts:\n- Oskar Schindler was born on 28 April 1908.\n- Abraham Bankier was born in 1910.\n- Abraham Bankier was one of the owners of the Rekord factory on Lipowa Street in Cracow, Poland.\n- During World War II, Oskar Schindler took over the Rekord factory.\n- Oskar Schindler was a German industrialist, spy, and member of the Nazi Party.\n- During the Holocaust, Oskar Schindler saved the lives of about 1,200 Jews by employing them in his enamelware and ammunitions factories in occupied Poland and the Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia.\n- Abraham Bankier died in 1956.\n- Oskar Schindler died on 9 October 1974.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
